# J9 done - Codemode: sandboxed JS that chains tools in one turn (gate-fix round 2)

## Summary

J9 adds the `codemode` agent tool: a short model-written JS program runs in a
QuickJS (WASM) sandbox and reaches the outside world only through
`tools.<name>(args)`, routed through Loam's existing tool registry and the same
approval/policy path as normal tool calls. Opt-in, off by default.

This session's gate failure was the parity merge aborting on an untracked local
`.jcode-done` marker; resolved by completing the merge (two rounds: 3c86ecf,
then 519f889 which landed O7 mid-session), resolving the single
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES conflict by keeping both sides, and committing. The
previously reported quickjs module-resolution failures (TS2307 / esbuild
"Could not resolve") are gone: both quickjs deps are in package.json +
package-lock.json and installed in node_modules on the merged tree.

## Test commands (all run from the worktree root)

- npx tsc --noEmit                      -> pass
- npm run build:server                  -> pass (dist/server.cjs ~21.6 MB)
- cd packages/web && npx next build     -> pass (25/25 static pages)
- npm run verify                        -> pass (typecheck, encoding, eval, orchestrator, recovery, modes)
- npm run check:eventlog                -> PASS (O7 checks a-d)
- node --import tsx --test "src/codemode/__tests__/*.test.ts" -> 46/46 pass
- node --import tsx --test src/server/__tests__/runTools.test.ts src/server/__tests__/dataControls.test.ts -> 21/21 pass
- cd packages/web && npx vitest run src/components/settings -> 50/50 pass
- node --import tsx --test "src/**/*.test.ts" -> 2988 tests, 2988 pass, 0 fail

## J9 acceptance evidence

- read+grep 20x fan-out: script makes 20 reads + 20 greps in one run; only the
  compact summary returns; transcript growth asserted < 2 KB (passes).
- No fs/net/process/timers in the sandbox; wall-clock timeout, memory limit,
  tool-call cap and policy-denied-tool-stays-denied all covered by passing tests.
- Bundling: the singlefile QuickJS variant inlines its wasm into the esbuild
  bundle (raw `\0asm` header present in dist/server.cjs as an escaped template
  literal). A throwaway esbuild probe (same bundling as build:server, deleted
  after the run) imported src/codemode/wasmLoader.ts, bundled to CJS, and
  evaluated `2 + 3` inside the sandbox from the bundle: result 5.

## RAM

No dedicated RAM benchmark was required for J9; the sandbox-level memory limit
is enforced and covered by the engine test suite (enforces the memory limit).
